  "narrative": "All newly delivered results are valid discovery Welch interaction contrasts. I interpreted them on the already signed claim scale: for a registered +1 direction, positive values indicate stronger association in the registered direction; for -1, positive values indicate a more negative raw exposed-minus-comparator interaction, i.e. stronger composite dependency for the exposed subgroup relative to the complement. Support requires the signed point estimate to be clearly above 0.15 units and the interval not to leave the threshold/direction question ambiguous. Most new effect-modification tests are null or wrong-signed. H312 (SMARCA4 loss x MYC high), H314 (MSI-high x MYC high), H317 (SMARCA4 loss x 8q24 gain), H319 (MSI-high x 8q24 gain), and H315 (PTEN loss x MYC high) have registered-direction point estimates far below threshold and intervals crossing zero; several have intervals extending into the opposite direction. H313 and H318 are wrong-signed or negligible for KEAP1 loss interactions, and H320 opposes the registered PTEN-loss-by-SMARCA4-loss direction. I therefore reject these as unsupported in the registered direction, not as proof of exact null effects. Technical-quality interactions are also unsupported: H38 (TP53 x screen_roc_auc high) is small and zero-crossing; H39 (TP53 x Cas9 activity high) is wrong-signed; H75 (SMARCA4 x screen quality) is wrong-signed/null; H76 (KEAP1 x screen quality) is wrong-signed and zero-crossing. The only potentially informative new signal is H316, TP53 loss x 8q24 copy gain, signed estimate +0.310 with interval +0.089 to +0.530. It is statistically positive and above threshold at the point estimate, but the lower bound remains below the 0.15-unit meaningful-effect threshold and it arises from a multiplicity-sensitive discovery interaction panel with no independent validation capacity remaining. I therefore keep H316 unresolved but close the investigation for this run; it does not warrant acceptance. Core dataset-level main associations remain unchanged: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss associate with higher composite score (weaker composite dependency), while SMARCA4 loss, MSI-high, and PTEN loss associate with lower raw composite score (stronger composite dependency), with PTEN loss the weakest accepted main effect. These remain associations in the supplied dataset only, not causal or external claims.",
  "research_notes": "Latest appraise: The MYC-high and 8q24-gain interaction panel mostly does not modify the accepted core main effects. Rejections are unsupported registered-direction interactions, not exact-zero claims. The only borderline finding is H316, TP53_loss x copy_number_8q24 >= 0.4, signed +0.310 [0.089, 0.530]. It is positive and statistically non-null but threshold-uncertain and not independently validated; mark unresolved/closed for this run. Technical screen-quality and Cas9-activity interaction probes H38, H39, H75, H76 are rejected, indicating no evidence that accepted core main effects differ meaningfully by these measured quality strata at the 0.15-unit threshold. H320 PTEN-loss-by-SMARCA4-loss reversal is also null/opposed and closed. Core accepted associations remain TP53 loss (higher composite / weaker dependency), KEAP1 loss (higher composite / weaker dependency), SMARCA4 loss (lower raw composite / stronger dependency), MSI-high (stronger dependency), and PTEN loss (weaker accepted main effect but still stronger dependency). All conclusions remain dataset-level associations; independent validation is exhausted."
